{"id":594,"name":"alomomola","speciesId":594,"dex":594,"form":"normal","generation":5,"types":["water"],"stats":{"hp":165,"attack":75,"defense":80,"special-attack":40,"special-defense":45,"speed":65},"abilities":[{"name":"healer","hidden":false},{"name":"hydration","hidden":false},{"name":"regenerator","hidden":true}],"height":12,"weight":316,"baseExp":165,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/594.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/594.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/594.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/594.ogg","genus":"Caring Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon carinhoso","flavor":[{"version":"black","text":"The special membrane enveloping Alomomola has the ability to heal wounds."},{"version":"white","text":"Floating in the open sea is how they live. When they find a wounded Pokémon, they embrace it and bring it to shore."},{"version":"black-2","text":"It gently holds injured and weak Pokémon in its fins. Its special membrane heals their wounds."},{"version":"sun","text":"It uses its special mucus to close the wounds of injured Pokémon. The reason for this behavior remains unknown."},{"version":"moon","text":"They float upon the open sea. Many water Pokémon gather in the area around Alomomola."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"Fishermen take them along on long voyages, because if you have an Alomomola with you, there’ll be no need for a doctor or medicine."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"The reason it helps Pokémon in a weakened condition is that any Pokémon coming after them may also attack Alomomola."}],"flavorPt":"A razão pela qual ajuda Pokémon enfraquecidos é que qualquer Pokémon que venha atrás deles também pode atacar Alomomola.","genderRate":4,"captureRate":75,"eggGroups":["water1","water2"],"isLege